{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J9eiHC5DSp78dwfDEjh4H3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I have thoroughly explored the codebase. Let me now compile a comprehensive report with all the findings.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. Full Directory Tree of `src/`\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── app/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   └── [...nextauth]/\n│   │   │       └── route.ts\n│   │   └── github/\n│   │       ├── jobs/\n│   │       │   └── [owner]/\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [runId]/\n│   │       │               └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── logs/\n│   │       │   └── [owner]/\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [jobId]/\n│   │       │               └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── orgs/\n│   │       │   └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── repos/\n│   │       │   └── [org]/\n│   │       │       └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── runs/\n│   │       │   └── [org]/\n│   │       │       ├── route.ts\n│   │       │       ├── summaries/\n│   │       │       │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [runId]/\n│   │       │               ├── cancel/\n│   │       │               │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │               ├── rerun/\n│   │       │               │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │               └── rerun-failed/\n│   │       │                   └── route.ts\n│   │       └── user/\n│   │           └── route.ts\n│   ├── favicon.ico\n│   ├── globals.css\n│   ├── layout.tsx\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── components/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   └── login-button.tsx\n│   ├── dashboard/\n│   │   ├── org-selector.tsx\n│   │   ├── status-badge.tsx\n│   │   ├── workflow-dashboard.tsx\n│   │   ├── workflow-jobs.tsx\n│   │   └── workflow-run-card.tsx\n│   ├── providers/\n│   │   └── session-provider.tsx\n│   └── ui/\n│       ├── alert.tsx\n│       ├── avatar.tsx\n│       ├── badge.tsx\n│       ├── button.tsx\n│       ├── card.tsx\n│       ├── collapsible.tsx\n│       ├── dialog.tsx\n│       ├── dropdown-menu.tsx\n│       ├── scroll-area.tsx\n│       ├── select.tsx\n│       ├── separator.tsx\n│       ├── skeleton.tsx\n│       ├── tabs.tsx\n│       └── tooltip.tsx\n├── lib/\n│   ├── api-error.ts\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   ├── github-route-error.ts\n│   ├── github.ts\n│   ├── utils.ts\n│   └── workflow-status.ts\n└── types/\n    └── next-auth.d.ts\n```\n\n### 2. Authentication Configuration (`src/lib/auth.ts`)\n\n**OAuth Provider:** GitHub OAuth via NextAuth.js\n\n**OAuth Scopes Requested:**\n- `read:user` - Read user profile information\n- `user:email` - Access email addresses\n- `read:org` - List organizations the user belongs to\n- `repo` - Access repositories (needed for Actions management)\n- `workflow` - Manage workflow runs (rerun, cancel, etc.)\n\n**Configuration:**\n```typescript\nGitHubProvider({\n  clientId: process.env.GITHUB_ID!,\n  clientSecret: process.env.GITHUB_SECRET!,\n  authorization: {\n    params: {\n      scope: \"read:user user:email read:org repo workflow\",\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Session Configuration:**\n- Uses JWT callback to store GitHub access token\n- Session callback adds access token to session object\n- Custom sign-in page: `/` (landing page)\n\n### 3. Main Dashboard Component (`src/components/dashboard/workflow-dashboard.tsx`)\n\n**View Modes:**\n- `cards` - Card-based grid layout (default)\n- `ops` - Operations view with compact table-like layout\n\n**Sorting Modes:**\n- `priority` - Priority-based (failures, active runs, queued) (default)\n- `newest` - Newest first (by creation date)\n- `oldest` - Oldest first (by creation date)\n- `duration` - Longest duration first\n- `queue-age` - Oldest queue age (for queued/waiting runs)\n- `repo` - Repository name A-Z\n\n**Grouping Modes:**\n- `none` - No grouping (default)\n- `repo` - Group by repository\n- `workflow` - Group by workflow name\n- `branch` - Group by branch\n- `status` - Group by status (Running, Failed, Queued, Successful)\n\n**Filtering Options:**\n- `all` - Show all workflow runs (default)\n- `running` - Only in-progress runs\n- `success` - Only successful runs\n- `failure` - Only failed runs\n- `queued` - Only queued/waiting runs\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Auto-refresh**: Automatically refreshes every 30 seconds (toggleable)\n- **Live status indicators**: Real-time updates with spinner animation\n- **Statistics cards**: Total, Running, Queued, Success, Failed counts\n- **Rate limit handling**: Detects GitHub API rate limits and pauses auto-refresh\n- **Expandable runs**: Click to expand and see job details\n- **Job summaries**: Automatically loads job summaries for:\n  - Expanded runs\n  - Active workflow runs\n  - Failed runs\n  - Top 20 runs in view\n- **Batch fetching**: Fetches job summaries in batches of 6\n- **Stale data warnings**: Shows alerts when background refresh fails\n- **Partial repository coverage**: Warns when some repos fail to load\n\n**Priority Scoring Algorithm:**\n```typescript\n- Failed runs: +1000 points\n- Each failed job: +50 points\n- In-progress runs: +650 points\n- Queued/waiting runs: +500 points + (queue age in minutes)\n- Each running job: +20 points\n- Each waiting/pending/queued job: +5 points\n```\n\n### 4. API Routes\n\n**Authentication:**\n- `POST /api/auth/[...nextauth]` - NextAuth.js authentication handler\n\n**User & Organization:**\n- `GET /api/github/user` - Get authenticated user info\n- `GET /api/github/orgs` - List user's organizations (includes personal account)\n\n**Repositories:**\n- `GET /api/github/repos/[org]` - Get repositories for org/user\n\n**Workflow Runs:**\n- `GET /api/github/runs/[org]` - Get all workflow runs across org repositories\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/summaries` - Batch fetch job summaries for multiple runs\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/rerun` - Re-run entire workflow\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/rerun-failed` - Re-run only failed jobs\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/cancel` - Cancel running workflow\n\n**Jobs:**\n- `GET /api/github/jobs/[owner]/[repo]/[runId]` - Get jobs for a specific workflow run\n\n**Logs:**\n- `GET /api/github/logs/[owner]/[repo]/[jobId]` - Get logs for a specific job\n\n### 5. Landing/Sign-In Page (`src/app/page.tsx`)\n\n**Landing Page Features:**\n- **Hero section** with gradient background\n- **App branding**: \"GitHub Actions Manager\" with Activity icon\n- **Tagline**: \"Monitor, manage, and optimize your GitHub Actions workflows across all your organizations from a single dashboard\"\n- **CTA buttons**: \n  - \"Sign in with GitHub\" (primary)\n  - \"Learn More\" (secondary, links to github.com)\n- **Features showcase** (6 cards):\n  1. Real-time Monitoring - Live status updates with auto-refresh\n  2. Quick Actions - Re-run, retry, cancel with one click\n  3. Multi-Repo Overview - See all runs across organization\n  4. Instant Logs - Access logs without leaving dashboard\n  5. Secure by Design - GitHub OAuth with minimal permissions\n  6. Status at a Glance - Clear visual indicators\n- **Footer**: \"Built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and the GitHub API\"\n\n**Authenticated View:**\n- Sticky header with app logo and user menu (LoginButton)\n- Main content area with WorkflowDashboard component\n- Max-width container (6xl) for readability\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Required Environment Variables:**\n\n1. **`GITHUB_ID`** (Required)\n   - GitHub OAuth App Client ID\n   - Source: GitHub Developer Settings → OAuth Apps\n   \n2. **`GITHUB_SECRET`** (Required)\n   - GitHub OAuth App Client Secret\n   - Source: GitHub Developer Settings → OAuth Apps\n\n3. **`NEXTAUTH_URL`** (Required)\n   - The canonical URL of your site\n   - Example: `http://localhost:3000` (development)\n   - Example: `https://yourdomain.com` (production)\n   - Used by NextAuth.js for callbacks\n\n4. **`NEXTAUTH_SECRET`** (Required)\n   - Secret key for encrypting tokens and session data\n   - Generate with: `openssl rand -base64 32`\n   - Must be a random string (at least 32 characters recommended)\n\n**No other environment variables are used in the codebase.**\n\n### 7. Technology Stack Summary\n\n**Framework & Core:**\n- Next.js 16.1.4 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n\n**Authentication:**\n- NextAuth.js 4.24.13\n- GitHub OAuth Provider\n\n**GitHub API:**\n- @octokit/rest 22.0.1 (Official GitHub SDK)\n\n**UI & Styling:**\n- Tailwind CSS 4\n- Radix UI components (shadcn/ui)\n- Lucide React (icons)\n- class-variance-authority (CVA)\n- clsx & tailwind-merge\n\n**Utilities:**\n- date-fns 4.1.0 (date formatting)\n\n**Development:**\n- ESLint (Next.js config)\n- @tailwindcss/postcss\n\n### 8. Key Project Files\n\n**Root Directory:**\n- `package.json` - Dependencies and scripts\n- `tsconfig.json` - TypeScript configuration\n- `next.config.ts` - Next.js configuration (minimal)\n- `components.json` - shadcn/ui configuration\n- `tailwind.config.ts` - Tailwind CSS configuration\n- `.gitignore` - Git ignore rules (includes .env*)\n- `README.md` - Existing documentation\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n- `npm run build` - Build for production\n- `npm start` - Start production server\n- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n\nThis comprehensive exploration should give you all the information needed to write an accurate and detailed README!"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab86475 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 57488\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 97735</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4433484f-60dd-42c7-bc8f-791da8f86c0a","uuid":"a572932a-0b5c-49d1-ac91-321f771eb667","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase at /home/dave/projects/github-actions-manager/.worktrees/feat-readme-build-it thoroughly.\n\nI need:\n\n1. A full directory tree (just file/folder names, not contents) of the `src/` directory and any other key directories\n2. The auth configuration — read `src/lib/auth.ts` or wherever NextAuth is configured, specifically looking for OAuth scopes\n3. The main dashboard component — look for the primary page component that shows workflow runs. Read it to understand the sorting modes, grouping modes, view modes, and filtering options available\n4. Any API routes — list all API route files under `src/app/api/`\n5. The landing/sign-in page component\n6. Any environment variable references — search for `process.env` usages to get a complete list of required env vars\n\nReturn all findings in detail so I can write an accurate README.","agentId":"ab86475","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I have thoroughly explored the codebase. Let me now compile a comprehensive report with all the findings.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. Full Directory Tree of `src/`\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── app/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   └── [...nextauth]/\n│   │   │       └── route.ts\n│   │   └── github/\n│   │       ├── jobs/\n│   │       │   └── [owner]/\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [runId]/\n│   │       │               └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── logs/\n│   │       │   └── [owner]/\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [jobId]/\n│   │       │               └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── orgs/\n│   │       │   └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── repos/\n│   │       │   └── [org]/\n│   │       │       └── route.ts\n│   │       ├── runs/\n│   │       │   └── [org]/\n│   │       │       ├── route.ts\n│   │       │       ├── summaries/\n│   │       │       │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │       └── [repo]/\n│   │       │           └── [runId]/\n│   │       │               ├── cancel/\n│   │       │               │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │               ├── rerun/\n│   │       │               │   └── route.ts\n│   │       │               └── rerun-failed/\n│   │       │                   └── route.ts\n│   │       └── user/\n│   │           └── route.ts\n│   ├── favicon.ico\n│   ├── globals.css\n│   ├── layout.tsx\n│   └── page.tsx\n├── components/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   └── login-button.tsx\n│   ├── dashboard/\n│   │   ├── org-selector.tsx\n│   │   ├── status-badge.tsx\n│   │   ├── workflow-dashboard.tsx\n│   │   ├── workflow-jobs.tsx\n│   │   └── workflow-run-card.tsx\n│   ├── providers/\n│   │   └── session-provider.tsx\n│   └── ui/\n│       ├── alert.tsx\n│       ├── avatar.tsx\n│       ├── badge.tsx\n│       ├── button.tsx\n│       ├── card.tsx\n│       ├── collapsible.tsx\n│       ├── dialog.tsx\n│       ├── dropdown-menu.tsx\n│       ├── scroll-area.tsx\n│       ├── select.tsx\n│       ├── separator.tsx\n│       ├── skeleton.tsx\n│       ├── tabs.tsx\n│       └── tooltip.tsx\n├── lib/\n│   ├── api-error.ts\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   ├── github-route-error.ts\n│   ├── github.ts\n│   ├── utils.ts\n│   └── workflow-status.ts\n└── types/\n    └── next-auth.d.ts\n```\n\n### 2. Authentication Configuration (`src/lib/auth.ts`)\n\n**OAuth Provider:** GitHub OAuth via NextAuth.js\n\n**OAuth Scopes Requested:**\n- `read:user` - Read user profile information\n- `user:email` - Access email addresses\n- `read:org` - List organizations the user belongs to\n- `repo` - Access repositories (needed for Actions management)\n- `workflow` - Manage workflow runs (rerun, cancel, etc.)\n\n**Configuration:**\n```typescript\nGitHubProvider({\n  clientId: process.env.GITHUB_ID!,\n  clientSecret: process.env.GITHUB_SECRET!,\n  authorization: {\n    params: {\n      scope: \"read:user user:email read:org repo workflow\",\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Session Configuration:**\n- Uses JWT callback to store GitHub access token\n- Session callback adds access token to session object\n- Custom sign-in page: `/` (landing page)\n\n### 3. Main Dashboard Component (`src/components/dashboard/workflow-dashboard.tsx`)\n\n**View Modes:**\n- `cards` - Card-based grid layout (default)\n- `ops` - Operations view with compact table-like layout\n\n**Sorting Modes:**\n- `priority` - Priority-based (failures, active runs, queued) (default)\n- `newest` - Newest first (by creation date)\n- `oldest` - Oldest first (by creation date)\n- `duration` - Longest duration first\n- `queue-age` - Oldest queue age (for queued/waiting runs)\n- `repo` - Repository name A-Z\n\n**Grouping Modes:**\n- `none` - No grouping (default)\n- `repo` - Group by repository\n- `workflow` - Group by workflow name\n- `branch` - Group by branch\n- `status` - Group by status (Running, Failed, Queued, Successful)\n\n**Filtering Options:**\n- `all` - Show all workflow runs (default)\n- `running` - Only in-progress runs\n- `success` - Only successful runs\n- `failure` - Only failed runs\n- `queued` - Only queued/waiting runs\n\n**Key Features:**\n- **Auto-refresh**: Automatically refreshes every 30 seconds (toggleable)\n- **Live status indicators**: Real-time updates with spinner animation\n- **Statistics cards**: Total, Running, Queued, Success, Failed counts\n- **Rate limit handling**: Detects GitHub API rate limits and pauses auto-refresh\n- **Expandable runs**: Click to expand and see job details\n- **Job summaries**: Automatically loads job summaries for:\n  - Expanded runs\n  - Active workflow runs\n  - Failed runs\n  - Top 20 runs in view\n- **Batch fetching**: Fetches job summaries in batches of 6\n- **Stale data warnings**: Shows alerts when background refresh fails\n- **Partial repository coverage**: Warns when some repos fail to load\n\n**Priority Scoring Algorithm:**\n```typescript\n- Failed runs: +1000 points\n- Each failed job: +50 points\n- In-progress runs: +650 points\n- Queued/waiting runs: +500 points + (queue age in minutes)\n- Each running job: +20 points\n- Each waiting/pending/queued job: +5 points\n```\n\n### 4. API Routes\n\n**Authentication:**\n- `POST /api/auth/[...nextauth]` - NextAuth.js authentication handler\n\n**User & Organization:**\n- `GET /api/github/user` - Get authenticated user info\n- `GET /api/github/orgs` - List user's organizations (includes personal account)\n\n**Repositories:**\n- `GET /api/github/repos/[org]` - Get repositories for org/user\n\n**Workflow Runs:**\n- `GET /api/github/runs/[org]` - Get all workflow runs across org repositories\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/summaries` - Batch fetch job summaries for multiple runs\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/rerun` - Re-run entire workflow\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/rerun-failed` - Re-run only failed jobs\n- `POST /api/github/runs/[org]/[repo]/[runId]/cancel` - Cancel running workflow\n\n**Jobs:**\n- `GET /api/github/jobs/[owner]/[repo]/[runId]` - Get jobs for a specific workflow run\n\n**Logs:**\n- `GET /api/github/logs/[owner]/[repo]/[jobId]` - Get logs for a specific job\n\n### 5. Landing/Sign-In Page (`src/app/page.tsx`)\n\n**Landing Page Features:**\n- **Hero section** with gradient background\n- **App branding**: \"GitHub Actions Manager\" with Activity icon\n- **Tagline**: \"Monitor, manage, and optimize your GitHub Actions workflows across all your organizations from a single dashboard\"\n- **CTA buttons**: \n  - \"Sign in with GitHub\" (primary)\n  - \"Learn More\" (secondary, links to github.com)\n- **Features showcase** (6 cards):\n  1. Real-time Monitoring - Live status updates with auto-refresh\n  2. Quick Actions - Re-run, retry, cancel with one click\n  3. Multi-Repo Overview - See all runs across organization\n  4. Instant Logs - Access logs without leaving dashboard\n  5. Secure by Design - GitHub OAuth with minimal permissions\n  6. Status at a Glance - Clear visual indicators\n- **Footer**: \"Built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and the GitHub API\"\n\n**Authenticated View:**\n- Sticky header with app logo and user menu (LoginButton)\n- Main content area with WorkflowDashboard component\n- Max-width container (6xl) for readability\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Required Environment Variables:**\n\n1. **`GITHUB_ID`** (Required)\n   - GitHub OAuth App Client ID\n   - Source: GitHub Developer Settings → OAuth Apps\n   \n2. **`GITHUB_SECRET`** (Required)\n   - GitHub OAuth App Client Secret\n   - Source: GitHub Developer Settings → OAuth Apps\n\n3. **`NEXTAUTH_URL`** (Required)\n   - The canonical URL of your site\n   - Example: `http://localhost:3000` (development)\n   - Example: `https://yourdomain.com` (production)\n   - Used by NextAuth.js for callbacks\n\n4. **`NEXTAUTH_SECRET`** (Required)\n   - Secret key for encrypting tokens and session data\n   - Generate with: `openssl rand -base64 32`\n   - Must be a random string (at least 32 characters recommended)\n\n**No other environment variables are used in the codebase.**\n\n### 7. Technology Stack Summary\n\n**Framework & Core:**\n- Next.js 16.1.4 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n\n**Authentication:**\n- NextAuth.js 4.24.13\n- GitHub OAuth Provider\n\n**GitHub API:**\n- @octokit/rest 22.0.1 (Official GitHub SDK)\n\n**UI & Styling:**\n- Tailwind CSS 4\n- Radix UI components (shadcn/ui)\n- Lucide React (icons)\n- class-variance-authority (CVA)\n- clsx & tailwind-merge\n\n**Utilities:**\n- date-fns 4.1.0 (date formatting)\n\n**Development:**\n- ESLint (Next.js config)\n- @tailwindcss/postcss\n\n### 8. Key Project Files\n\n**Root Directory:**\n- `package.json` - Dependencies and scripts\n- `tsconfig.json` - TypeScript configuration\n- `next.config.ts` - Next.js configuration (minimal)\n- `components.json` - shadcn/ui configuration\n- `tailwind.config.ts` - Tailwind CSS configuration\n- `.gitignore` - Git ignore rules (includes .env*)\n- `README.md` - Existing documentation\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n- `npm run build` - Build for production\n- `npm start` - Start production server\n- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n\nThis comprehensive exploration should give you all the information needed to write an accurate and detailed README!"}],"totalDurationMs":97735,"totalTokens":57488,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage